WEBVTT

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:05.312
TO_CHAR converts a typed date or timestamp into formatted text.

00:00:05.312 --> 00:00:09.022
This is useful for reports, labels, exports, and human-facing displays.

00:00:09.022 --> 00:00:17.972
But once you turn a timestamp into arbitrary text, temporal sorting and arithmetic become less direct.

00:00:17.972 --> 00:00:24.027
Keep the value typed through analytical processing and format it near the reporting boundary.

00:00:24.027 --> 00:00:31.452
Parsing converts text into a typed value; formatting converts a typed value into presentation text.

00:00:31.452 --> 00:00:38.027
Perform analytical work on typed dates and timestamps, then format near the presentation layer.

00:00:38.027 --> 00:00:44.482
If parsing can fail, validate the incoming pattern first instead of letting one malformed value stop an entire

00:00:44.482 --> 00:00:45.760
load.
